<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Compacts of Basel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1436</span> · Also known as Basel Compacts, Compactata · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussite-wars">Hussite Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Compacts of Basel were an agreement between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-basel">Council of Basel</a> and the moderate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussites">Hussites</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>, proclaimed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihlava">Jihlava</a> in 1436. They allowed communion in both kinds, bread and wine, to the laity in the Czech lands, making the Utraquist church the first to win formal recognition while rejecting papal practice. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-ii">Pope Pius II</a> repudiated them in 1462, but they remained the basis of Utraquist claims.</p></div>
